From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:14:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] plugins, targets: a user-access window owned by the access,
 not latched per vCPU

The user_access_window hooks (arm DACR, ppc AMR, x86 AC, riscv SUM) kept the
saved value and an open flag in the CPU.  A plugin access that raised a
guest fault left the latch open across the longjmp, and nothing reset it on
CPU reset or loadvm; an extable fixup or a task migration then restored a
stale DACR/AMR, or clac'ed, inside the guest's own copy_*_user (an oops, a
spurious -EFAULT, or PAN/SMAP left off).

The target hooks are now stateless: open returns the value to restore in
*saved and reports whether it opened anything.  The plugin access keeps it.
When the access raises a fault with the window open, the window stays open
for the guest's fixup and is recorded in cpu->uaccess_pend under the access's
key (its return address into the block, or the guest PC on the hw path); the
re-run adopts and closes it.  A pending window nobody adopts is dropped at
the next open that finds the window shut, on reset and on loadvm.

Review blocker 5.
